<BaseLayout title="Cost of Raising a Child Calculator: Birth to 18 | DollarAngle" description="Free child raising cost calculator. Estimate expenses from birth to 18 by childcare, public or private schooling, inflation and household budget.">
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}/>
<div class="container tool-page"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › <a href="/tools">Money Tools</a> › Cost of Raising a Child</nav>
<header class="intro"><p class="kicker">FREE FAMILY PLANNING CALCULATOR</p><h1>Cost of Raising a Child: <span>Project Your Family Budget to Age 18</span></h1><p>What might it cost to raise a child over the next 18 years? Explore editable spending assumptions and see how childcare, schooling and inflation change the total.</p></header>
<ChildCostProjector/>
<article class="guide"><h2>How does the child cost calculator work?</h2><p>The projection combines incremental housing, food, clothing, healthcare, childcare through age five and school tuition from ages six to seventeen. It adjusts expenses by age, your selected annual inflation assumption and the number of children. The results are scenarios, not official published regional averages.</p>
<h2>Why location and lifestyle matter</h2><p>Daycare, rent, school fees and healthcare differ widely even within the same country. Rather than assume a single national figure applies to your family, replace the example estimates with your local quotes and household spending plans. Currency selection changes formatting, not exchange rates.</p>
<h2>What is not included?</h2><p>The model excludes university education, parental lost earnings, tax credits, public benefits and changing household structure. It treats costs as additive for each child even though siblings may share certain expenses. For planning, try both conservative and higher-cost scenarios.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>{faq.map(([q,a])=><details><summary>{q}</summary><p>{a}</p></details>)}
<h2>Related DollarAngle tools</h2><p><a href="/tools/stay-at-home-parent-calculator">Compare childcare versus working costs →</a> <a href="/tools/mine-yours-ours-budget-calculator">Build a shared family budget →</a></p>
<p class="note">Educational illustration only. DollarAngle does not claim these preset assumptions are surveyed regional prices. The calculated spending is not personalized financial advice.</p></article></div>
</BaseLayout>
